{"schema":"learning-v2-theory.v1","lesson":7,"lang":"pl","title":"Pytania i «nie» o nawykach","sections":[{"num":"01","title":"Czego się nauczysz","defaultOpen":true,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"W lekcji 6 mówiłeś, co ludzie robią: I work, she cooks. Teraz nauczysz się pytać — «pracujesz w fabryce?», «gdzie parkujesz?» — mówić «nie» — «nie plotkuję» — i dodawać «zwykle» i «często»."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"Do you work in a factory?","translation":"Pracujesz w fabryce?","hi":"Do"},{"en":"Does the salon close late?","translation":"Czy salon zamyka się późno?","hi":"Does"},{"en":"I don't gossip.","translation":"Nie plotkuję.","hi":"don't"},{"en":"Where do you park?","translation":"Gdzie parkujesz?","hi":"Where do"},{"en":"I usually recycle.","translation":"Zwykle segreguję śmieci.","hi":"usually"}]}]},{"num":"02","title":"Pytanie zaczyna się od Do","defaultOpen":true,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Po polsku wystarczy «czy» albo sam głos: «Pracujesz w fabryce?». Po angielsku potrzebne jest małe Do na początku: Do you work in a factory? Do działa trochę jak «czy», a sama czynność się nie zmienia."},{"kind":"formula","formula":[{"text":"Do","accent":true},{"text":"you / they / we","accent":true},{"text":"czynność","accent":false},{"text":"?","accent":true}]},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"Do you work in a factory?","translation":"Pracujesz w fabryce?","hi":"Do"},{"en":"Do they send packages?","translation":"Czy oni wysyłają paczki?","hi":"Do"},{"en":"Do you have a menu?","translation":"Macie menu?","hi":"Do"},{"en":"Do you work at night?","translation":"Pracujesz w nocy?","hi":"Do"},{"en":"Do they check tickets here?","translation":"Czy tu sprawdzają bilety?","hi":"Do"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"You work in a factory?","right":"Do you work in a factory?"},{"wrong":"Work you in a factory?","right":"Do you work in a factory?"},{"wrong":"Have you a menu?","right":"Do you have a menu?"}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"word_bank","kind":"word_bank","prompt":"Zapytaj: «Pracujesz w fabryce?»","answer":["Do","you","work","in","a","factory"],"distractors":["Are","works"]}}]},{"num":"03","title":"Does — o he, she i jednej osobie","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Jeśli pytasz o he, she, it albo jedną osobę — the barber, the fan — zamiast Do stawiasz Does. A s, które miała czynność (he works), przechodzi na does i z czynności znika: Does he work?"},{"kind":"formula","formula":[{"text":"Does","accent":true},{"text":"he / she / it / jedna osoba","accent":true},{"text":"czynność bez s","accent":false},{"text":"?","accent":true}]},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"Does the barber work here?","translation":"Czy fryzjer tu pracuje?","hi":"Does"},{"en":"Does the fan work?","translation":"Czy wiatrak działa?","hi":"Does"},{"en":"Does he play chess?","translation":"Czy on gra w szachy?","hi":"Does"},{"en":"Does she play tennis?","translation":"Czy ona gra w tenisa?","hi":"Does"},{"en":"Does the cafe serve sushi?","translation":"Czy w kawiarni podają sushi?","hi":"Does"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"Does he plays chess?","right":"Does he play chess?"},{"wrong":"Do the fan work?","right":"Does the fan work?"},{"wrong":"Does she plays tennis?","right":"Does she play tennis?"}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"choice","kind":"choice","before":"Does the metro","after":"late?","options":["run","runs","running"],"answer":"run","why":"s już przeszło na does, czynność jest bez s."}}]},{"num":"04","title":"Do czy is?","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Jeśli w pytaniu jest czynność — potrzebne Do albo Does: Do they fix lamps? Jeśli czynności nie ma, a pytasz, kim ktoś jest albo jaki jest — potrzebne am, is, are, jak w lekcji 2: Are you a plumber? Do i is razem nie idą."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"Are you a plumber?","translation":"Jesteś hydraulikiem?","hi":"Are"},{"en":"Do they fix lamps?","translation":"Czy naprawiają lampy?","hi":"Do"},{"en":"Is the lesson difficult?","translation":"Czy lekcja jest trudna?","hi":"Is"},{"en":"Does the vet start early?","translation":"Czy weterynarz zaczyna wcześnie?","hi":"Does"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"Do you a plumber?","right":"Are you a plumber?"},{"wrong":"Are they fix lamps?","right":"Do they fix lamps?"}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"binary","kind":"binary","question":"Chcesz wiedzieć, czy warsztat naprawia lampy. Które zdanie jest poprawne?","optionA":"Are they fix lamps?","optionB":"Do they fix lamps?","correct":"B","explain":"Jest czynność fix, więc Do."}}]},{"num":"05","title":"«Nie»: don't i doesn't","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Po polsku «nie» stoi tuż przed czynnością: «nie plotkuję». Po angielsku potrzebne jest don't — z I, you, we, they — albo doesn't — z he, she, it i jedną osobą. A z doesn't czynność traci s: He doesn't have a house."},{"kind":"formula","formula":[{"text":"kto","accent":true},{"text":"don't / doesn't","accent":true},{"text":"czynność bez s","accent":false}]},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"I don't gossip.","translation":"Nie plotkuję.","hi":"don't"},{"en":"I don't brag.","translation":"Nie przechwalam się.","hi":"don't"},{"en":"I don't have money.","translation":"Nie mam pieniędzy.","hi":"don't"},{"en":"He doesn't have a house.","translation":"On nie ma domu.","hi":"doesn't"},{"en":"The horn doesn't work.","translation":"Klakson nie działa.","hi":"doesn't"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"I not gossip.","right":"I don't gossip."},{"wrong":"He don't have a house.","right":"He doesn't have a house."},{"wrong":"He doesn't has a house.","right":"He doesn't have a house."},{"wrong":"The horn doesn't works.","right":"The horn doesn't work."}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"spot_slip","kind":"spot_slip","chips":["The","horn","doesn't","works"],"answerIndex":3,"hint":"Jedno słowo ma zbędną końcówkę. Dotknij go.","fix":"Po doesn't czynność jest bez s: The horn doesn't work."}}]},{"num":"06","title":"There is no — «nie ma tu»","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Żeby powiedzieć, że czegoś tu nie ma, wygodne jest There is no: There is no courier here — «nie ma tu kuriera». Dla kilku rzeczy — There are no. Po no nie stawia się ani a, ani any."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"There is no courier here.","translation":"Nie ma tu kuriera.","hi":"no"},{"en":"There is no tape here.","translation":"Nie ma tu taśmy.","hi":"no"},{"en":"There is no bus in the morning.","translation":"Rano nie ma autobusu.","hi":"no"},{"en":"There are no pliers here.","translation":"Nie ma tu kombinerek.","hi":"no"},{"en":"There is no guard at the gate.","translation":"Przy bramie nie ma ochroniarza.","hi":"no"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"Not is courier here.","right":"There is no courier here."},{"wrong":"There is not courier here.","right":"There is no courier here."},{"wrong":"There is no a courier here.","right":"There is no courier here."}]},{"kind":"tip","text":"There isn't a courier here znaczy to samo, znasz to z lekcji 4. There is no brzmi trochę stanowczej."}]},{"num":"07","title":"Gdzie i kiedy: Where do…? When does…?","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Żeby zapytać «gdzie» albo «kiedy», Where lub When idzie na sam początek, a dalej wszystko jak w zwykłym pytaniu: do albo does, kto, czynność. Po polsku «Gdzie pracujesz?» bez do, ale po angielsku: Where do you work?"},{"kind":"formula","formula":[{"text":"Where / When","accent":true},{"text":"do / does","accent":true},{"text":"kto","accent":true},{"text":"czynność","accent":false},{"text":"?","accent":true}]},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"Where do you work?","translation":"Gdzie pracujesz?","hi":"Where do"},{"en":"Where do you park?","translation":"Gdzie parkujesz?","hi":"Where do"},{"en":"When does the rink close?","translation":"Kiedy zamykają lodowisko?","hi":"When does"},{"en":"When do you have lunch?","translation":"Kiedy jesz obiad?","hi":"When do"},{"en":"When does she harvest apples?","translation":"Kiedy ona zbiera jabłka?","hi":"When does"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"Where you work?","right":"Where do you work?"},{"wrong":"When the rink closes?","right":"When does the rink close?"},{"wrong":"When does she harvests apples?","right":"When does she harvest apples?"}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"choice","kind":"choice","before":"When","after":"the rink close?","options":["do","does","is"],"answer":"does","why":"Lodowisko jest jedno, jak he albo she, więc does."}}]},{"num":"08","title":"usually i often — przed czynnością","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"usually — «zwykle», often — «często». Stawia się je tuż przed czynnością: I usually recycle, I often iron shirts. Po polsku można «prasuję często koszule», ale po angielsku often stoi tylko przed iron."},{"kind":"formula","formula":[{"text":"kto","accent":true},{"text":"usually / often","accent":true},{"text":"czynność","accent":false}]},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"I usually recycle.","translation":"Zwykle segreguję śmieci.","hi":"usually"},{"en":"I often iron shirts.","translation":"Często prasuję koszule.","hi":"often"},{"en":"She often dusts the shelves.","translation":"Często ściera kurz z półek.","hi":"often"},{"en":"I usually unplug the kettle.","translation":"Zwykle wyłączam czajnik z kontaktu.","hi":"usually"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"I iron often shirts.","right":"I often iron shirts."},{"wrong":"She often dust the shelves.","right":"She often dusts the shelves."},{"wrong":"I usually recycles.","right":"I usually recycle."}]},{"kind":"tip","text":"usually i often niczego nie zmieniają: po she czynność dalej dostaje s — she often dusts."},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"binary","kind":"binary","question":"Mówisz o sobie. Które zdanie jest poprawne?","optionA":"I iron often shirts.","optionB":"I often iron shirts.","correct":"B","explain":"often stoi tuż przed czynnością iron."}}]},{"num":"09","title":"«Często…?» — Do you often…?","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"W pytaniu often stoi tam samo — przed czynnością, po kto: Do you often forget the key? Does your brother often miss the bus? Najpierw Do albo Does, potem kto, potem often, potem czynność."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"Do you often forget the key?","translation":"Często zapominasz klucza?","hi":"often"},{"en":"Does your brother often miss the bus?","translation":"Czy twój brat często spóźnia się na autobus?","hi":"often"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"Do often you forget the key?","right":"Do you often forget the key?"},{"wrong":"Does your brother often misses the bus?","right":"Does your brother often miss the bus?"}]}]},{"num":"10","title":"Błędy, które robi prawie każdy","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"You work in a factory?","right":"Do you work in a factory?"},{"wrong":"Are you work here?","right":"Do you work here?"},{"wrong":"Does he plays chess?","right":"Does he play chess?"},{"wrong":"I not gossip.","right":"I don't gossip."},{"wrong":"He don't have a house.","right":"He doesn't have a house."},{"wrong":"Not is courier here.","right":"There is no courier here."},{"wrong":"Where you work?","right":"Where do you work?"},{"wrong":"I iron often shirts.","right":"I often iron shirts."}]},{"kind":"tip","text":"Główna zasada lekcji: s jest tylko w jednym miejscu. Jest does albo doesn't — czynność bez s. Nie ma does — czynność z s po he i she."}]},{"num":"11","title":"Co zabrać do ćwiczeń","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Pytanie — Do albo Does na początku. «Nie» — don't albo doesn't przed czynnością. Po does i doesn't czynność bez s. «Nie ma tu» — There is no. Gdzie i kiedy — Where, When + do / does. «Zwykle» i «często» — tuż przed czynnością."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"Do they work on weekends?","translation":"Czy pracują w weekendy?","hi":"Do"},{"en":"Does the coach leave early?","translation":"Czy autokar odjeżdża wcześnie?","hi":"Does"},{"en":"He doesn't have a house.","translation":"On nie ma domu.","hi":"doesn't"},{"en":"When does the rink close?","translation":"Kiedy zamykają lodowisko?","hi":"When does"},{"en":"She often dusts the shelves.","translation":"Często ściera kurz z półek.","hi":"often"}]}]}],"sessionSection":{"1":"02","2":"02","3":"02","4":"02","5":"02","6":"04","7":"02","8":"02","9":"03","10":"03","11":"03","12":"03","13":"03","14":"03","15":"03","16":"03","17":"05","18":"05","19":"06","20":"06","21":"06","22":"06","23":"06","24":"06","25":"07","26":"07","27":"07","28":"07","29":"07","30":"07","31":"07","32":"07","33":"08","34":"08","35":"08","36":"08","37":"08","38":"08","39":"08","40":"08","41":"08","42":"08","43":"08","44":"08","45":"08","46":"08","47":"08","48":"08","49":"08","50":"08","51":"09","52":"09","53":"09","54":"09","55":"09","56":"09"}}
